WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.920
Cochlear implant candidacy is more than a hearing threshold.

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:12.480
The team considers hearing loss, benefit from appropriately fitted hearing aids, functional progress, medical suitability, and the support needed for rehabilitation.

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:23.500
The lecture describes the youngest group, nine to twenty-four months, has bilateral profound sensorineural loss and limited development of auditory skills with hearing aids.

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:32.520
For older children, the slide describes bilateral severe-to-profound loss and thirty percent or less on open-set words in the best-aided condition.

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:34.870
That is the slide's wording.

00:00:35.415 --> 00:00:41.495
Do not transfer it to every manufacturer or every single-sided-deafness case.

00:00:41.795 --> 00:00:47.875
The packet contains conflicting single-sided-deafness percentages, so those remain unresolved.

00:00:48.645 --> 00:00:53.445
An SLP can still refer a child whose listening and language progress has stalled.

00:00:53.995 --> 00:00:57.035
A referral starts a full evaluation.

00:00:57.430 --> 00:01:00.230
It does not guarantee that the child qualifies.

